          "title": "You'll want to know: le règlement",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le règlement — \"the regulations, the rules; the payment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le règlement de l'école interdit les téléphones en classe. The school rules forbid phones in class."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also means payment: règlement par carte."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "règlement is built from régler \"to regulate, to settle\" and -ment. The verb rests on règle \"rule\", from Latin rēgula \"a ruler, a rule\", built on regere \"to guide\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
